driven solutions, including intelligence analytics, space system development, cybersecurity, and IT to the federal government and commercial clients. The Global Engineering Solutions segment provides large-scale environmental remediation, nuclear power solutions, platform engineering, sustainment, and supply chain management for the U.S. government and allied nations. It serves energy and environment, defense, civilian, space, and commercial markets. The company operates in Australia, Belgium, Canada, the Czechia, France, Japan, Lithuania, the Netherlands, Norway, Oman, Poland, Slovakia, South Africa, the United Kingdom, and internationally. Amentum Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 2023 and is headquartered in Chantilly, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John E. Heller | CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 45K people. Revenue per employee of $307K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 28%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $13K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $733 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Amentum Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $6.0B market cap on $13.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +28% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $583M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.86\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Goodwill represents 51% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at 